// Aggregate grouping with an extra body variable (BENCH-135's grouping regression, `vote_cnt` 2 in Molly's provenance
// suite, R06 §12.6), written for this corpus. The voters p and q each send their ballot to the teller t at time 1.
// `turnout` groups by the teller only, although its body also binds the voter P, so turnout(t, 2) holds from time 2
// with both ballots as contributors, and losing either ballot falsifies it. An implementation that also grouped by P
// would derive turnout(t, 1) instead. Blossom golden corpus, re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

ballot(T, P)@async :- cast(P, T);
ballot(T, P)@next :- ballot(T, P);
roster(T, P, Id)@next :- roster(T, P, Id);

turnout(T, count<Id>) :- ballot(T, P), roster(T, P, Id);

// pre: the teller's registered ids; post: each of them, once both ballots are counted in one group (turnout(t, 2))
pre(T, Id) :- roster(T, P, Id);
post(T, Id) :- turnout(T, N), roster(T, P, Id), N == 2;

roster("t", "p", 1)@1;
roster("t", "q", 2)@1;
cast("p", "t")@1;
cast("q", "t")@1;
